This directory is deliberately empty.

Vercel serves this project's "output directory" as static files, and anything
it finds here is served *instead of* being proxied — the filesystem is checked
before rewrites. An empty directory means every path falls through to the
rewrite in vercel.json, which is the whole point of the project.

It cannot simply be deleted. With the framework preset set to "Other" and no
`public` directory present, Vercel falls back to serving the repository root,
which would publish package.json, the source tree and docs/ at
aurabank.vercel.app — and shadow the proxy for those paths.
